{"lines":[{"w":0.07911034901936842,"h":0.016475076914908349,"x":0.79879069015362014,"c":1,"t":"Reading","y":0.070977577661736957},{"t":"production significantly, and so enslaved many other members of the Ceylonese native","y":0.1117716031405257,"x":0.082496473722756508,"w":0.77674530029296873,"h":0.028870357211297826,"c":1},{"w":0.77484588623046879,"h":0.02962875857479097,"c":1,"x":0.082484366224823968,"t":"population, forcing them to work in cinnamon harvesting. In 1518, the Portuguese built","y":0.1293857853232081},{"h":0.030465568793027198,"y":0.14746470507608889,"c":1,"t":"a fort on Ceylon, which enabled them to protect the island, so helping them to develop a","x":0.080594332134158536,"w":0.78994313557942719},{"y":0.16662285311906022,"x":0.080610563608051869,"t":"monopoly in the cinnamon trade and generate very high profits. In the late 16th century,","w":0.78810089111328141,"h":0.029435155933623336,"c":1},{"y":0.18361021058516969,"t":"for example, they enjoyed a tenfold profit when shipping cinnamon over a journey of","w":0.75614013671875002,"c":1,"h":0.029601213169036522,"x":0.078696617217555151},{"w":0.28759399414062498,"h":0.018895348808647183,"t":"eight days from Ceylon to India.","c":1,"x":0.080827062924400839,"y":0.20494186044987339},{"y":0.23963222148262897,"w":0.72980321248372393,"h":0.026856618317495418,"x":0.080584044616962558,"t":"When the Dutch arrived off the coast of southern Asia at the very beginning of the","c":1},{"y":0.25711885285852643,"c":1,"h":0.028340216229519211,"t":"17th century, they set their sights on displacing the Portuguese as kings of cinnamon.","w":0.76751556396484366,"x":0.080555567932479921},{"h":0.0263575168862622,"c":1,"t":"The Dutch allied themselves with Kandy, an inland kingdom on Ceylon. In return","x":0.080551307980824924,"y":0.27627451336813724,"w":0.71855717976888023},{"c":1,"w":0.72409342447916658,"h":0.024691874644714895,"t":"for payments of elephants and cinnamon, they protected the native king from the","x":0.07873955328019927,"y":0.29528729774041951},{"c":1,"w":0.76551462809244797,"h":0.026057533809467848,"y":0.31344459448115303,"t":"Portuguese. By 1640, the Dutch broke the 150-year Portuguese monopoly when they","x":0.080608476123108994},{"w":0.73171752929687495,"c":1,"h":0.028663920189439307,"t":"overran and occupied their factories. By 1658, they had permanently expelled the","x":0.078695895808246707,"y":0.33130764419282022},{"w":0.75048950195312503,"t":"Portuguese from the island, thereby gaining control of the lucrative cinnamon trade.","h":0.02623260335928379,"x":0.080587076836848348,"c":1,"y":0.3506812470907853},{"w":0.78622365315755205,"t":"In order to protect their hold on the market, the Dutch, like the Portuguese before them,","y":0.38736315613858496,"x":0.078688726216333479,"h":0.026688715141969466,"c":1},{"x":0.078708402526047216,"y":0.40532151111107839,"w":0.74669896443684891,"h":0.0248303655954768,"t":"treated the native inhabitants harshly. Because of the need to boost production and","c":1},{"t":"satisfy Europe's ever-increasing appetite for cinnamon, the Dutch began to alter the","h":0.024619728230846682,"c":1,"y":0.42526531190061845,"x":0.078761035105498728,"w":0.7522300720214844},{"c":1,"y":0.44227262089147823,"t":"harvesting practices of the Ceylonese. Over time, the supply of cinnamon trees on the","w":0.77302627563476567,"h":0.02654461636515637,"x":0.078688101457948398},{"x":0.078789099616633107,"y":0.46200385654412357,"w":0.78978902180989574,"c":1,"t":"island became nearly exhausted, due to systematic stripping of the bark. Eventually, the","h":0.023769599732781588},{"x":0.080621101432019102,"w":0.79546040852864586,"h":0.024724015864109994,"c":1,"y":0.47897330992078613,"t":"Dutch began cultivating their own cinnamon trees to supplement the diminishing number"},{"y":0.49673540153283513,"w":0.26951398213704425,"c":1,"x":0.07863000521700475,"h":0.020885578064632981,"t":"of wild trees available for use."},{"y":0.53576075605621176,"t":"Then, in 1796, the English arrived on Ceylon, thereby displacing the Dutch from their","w":0.76145634969075526,"c":1,"x":0.078854139486001881,"h":0.021569177709850895},{"t":"control of the cinnamon monopoly. By the middle of the 19th century, production of","h":0.024498125851269426,"w":0.74098027547200529,"x":0.078771076494857081,"c":1,"y":0.55224555832177424},{"t":"cinnamon reached 1,000 tons a year, after a lower grade quality of the spice became","c":1,"x":0.078762579365243349,"h":0.024864189408321358,"y":0.57109393969618005,"w":0.76164896647135416},{"t":"acceptable to European tastes. By that time, cinnamon was being grown in other parts","h":0.022538845261219409,"c":1,"x":0.078809400939765628,"w":0.77470774332682291,"y":0.59143869646945113},{"h":0.02246670990088484,"t":"of the Indian Ocean region and in the West Indies, Brazil, and Guyana. Not only was a","w":0.77472900390624999,"x":0.078798700417640366,"c":1,"y":0.60889913619854963},{"t":"monopoly of cinnamon becoming impossible, but the spice trade overall was diminishing","y":0.62689584052071479,"h":0.022901629603300555,"w":0.79538950602213543,"x":0.07880639403550295,"c":1},{"y":0.64268909727950985,"w":0.79763748168945314,"c":1,"h":0.028932211557205378,"x":0.076765873344008834,"t":"in economic potential, and was eventually superseded by the rise of trade in coffee, tea,"},{"h":0.022396149055004422,"c":1,"y":0.66369697034569164,"w":0.19298615773518879,"x":0.078330108116871369,"t":"chocolate, and sugar."},{"w":0.028195489247639927,"t":"39","y":0.9694767443199136,"x":0.84586466128014459,"h":0.014534883321060788,"c":1}],"h":3106,"w":2400}